# S195 T21 — vitest snapshots are written with LF by vitest itself. With `core.autocrlf=true` (this
# project's Windows checkouts) git checked them out CRLF, so every full vitest run rewrote
# `src/state/spawners/__snapshots__/pentagramBuildability.test.ts.snap` EOL-only and left the tree
# dirty (`git status` M, `git diff` empty). Pinning them to LF in the working copy makes vitest's
# write a byte-for-byte no-op. Index content is unchanged (it was already LF).
*.snap text eol=lf

# S196 (s196/ci HIGH-1) - every .mjs is checked out LF. A `#!` shebang line followed by CRLF is a
# SyntaxError when vitest dynamically imports the file (`src/ci.watchdog.test.ts`, `src/ci.verifyDeploy.test.ts`
# import ci-watchdog.mjs / verify-deploy.mjs): 24 of 25 red on every core.autocrlf=true checkout. The
# shebangs are gone too (both files are only run as `node <file>`); this rule is the second wall.
*.mjs text eol=lf
